WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.195 --> 00:00:04.028
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.028 --> 00:00:06.830
Today I'm going to talk about
the seven things you must do

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.381
to achieve your goals.

00:00:09.381 --> 00:00:11.121
- [Computer Voice] Nine.

00:00:11.121 --> 00:00:11.954
Eight.

00:00:11.954 --> 00:00:15.520
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:16.353
Seven.

00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:18.814
- So one of the things I find
with a lot of entrepreneurs

00:00:18.814 --> 00:00:19.861
is we set goals, right.

00:00:19.861 --> 00:00:21.527
We have goals, upon goals, upon goals,

00:00:21.527 --> 00:00:23.534
we have to-do lists a mile high

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:24.910
and we just keep setting goals

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.121
and we don't necessarily
actually follow through

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:28.406
or achieve them.

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:29.648
And so tody I'm going to share with you

00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:33.815
my seven ways to actually
get your goals accomplished.

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:38.309
Number one is set the right goals.

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:39.358
This is really important.

00:00:39.358 --> 00:00:42.412
A lot of times we don't
set the right goals for us.

00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:45.244
We set the goals that
we think we should do

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.805
or that other people want for us,

00:00:46.805 --> 00:00:49.374
but not the ones that are
actually right for us.

00:00:49.374 --> 00:00:51.434
I think of an example
when I was listening to

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.596
an audiobook on goal setting

00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:56.175
and the speaker was talking about,

00:00:56.175 --> 00:00:57.770
in a really passionate manner,

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:59.262
write down all your goals.

00:00:59.262 --> 00:01:02.667
If you want to be a painter,
write down create a masterpiece.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.585
If you want to make a
sculpture, write that down,

00:01:04.585 --> 00:01:05.528
create a sculpture.

00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:08.799
If you want to write a score
for a song, write that down.

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:10.361
And we go, oh wow, that
sounds so interesting.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:11.194
I want to do that.

00:01:11.194 --> 00:01:12.984
I want to paint something, why not?

00:01:12.984 --> 00:01:13.966
I want to make a sculpture.

00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:15.200
Yeah, it's awesome.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.222
And then I come back to it
and I realize, you know what?

00:01:17.222 --> 00:01:19.322
I don't actually want to make a sculpture.

00:01:19.322 --> 00:01:20.798
I got kind of wrapped up in the moment,

00:01:20.798 --> 00:01:22.838
listening to the
excitement of this speaker,

00:01:22.838 --> 00:01:23.671
but it wasn't something

00:01:23.671 --> 00:01:25.612
that I actually deep down wanted to do

00:01:25.612 --> 00:01:26.766
and so you really want to make sure

00:01:26.766 --> 00:01:28.149
that the goals you set for yourself

00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:30.622
are ones that even when you come back to

00:01:30.622 --> 00:01:33.703
a week later, a month later,
still resonate with you.

00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:35.398
Like, the goal has to mean something.

00:01:35.398 --> 00:01:36.834
If you don't care about the goal

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.055
and actually accomplishing it,

00:01:38.055 --> 00:01:39.559
or if you're doing it
just for somebody else

00:01:39.559 --> 00:01:41.434
and it doesn't really
mean something to you,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.088
then you're never going to follow through.

00:01:43.088 --> 00:01:46.098
So I'd really force
you to audit your goals

00:01:46.098 --> 00:01:47.441
and look at them and examine them

00:01:47.441 --> 00:01:50.344
and think, do these actually excite me?

00:01:50.344 --> 00:01:53.570
Do I have the right goals
that I want to build around

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.545
and then you can focus on worrying about

00:01:55.545 --> 00:01:57.712
the steps to achieve them.

00:02:00.582 --> 00:02:02.500
Number two is have an important why.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.537
And this aligns closely
with the first one.

00:02:04.537 --> 00:02:06.471
Why is this so important?

00:02:06.471 --> 00:02:08.727
Why is it so important that you go out

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:10.766
and accomplish that goal?

00:02:10.766 --> 00:02:12.082
It has to come from a deep reason

00:02:12.082 --> 00:02:13.158
that really resonates with you,

00:02:13.158 --> 00:02:14.836
otherwise it's just
going to be a wishlist.

00:02:14.836 --> 00:02:16.437
And we all have a wishlist.

00:02:16.437 --> 00:02:19.107
We all have, again, that
to-do list that's a mile high

00:02:19.107 --> 00:02:21.674
and the ones that you actually, deeply,

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:22.510
meaningfully care about,

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.145
you have a strong why attached to it,

00:02:24.145 --> 00:02:25.755
those are the ones that
you're going to do.

00:02:25.755 --> 00:02:27.461
Too often, though, we only do the things

00:02:27.461 --> 00:02:28.628
that we're forced to do.

00:02:28.628 --> 00:02:31.374
You do it because a
customer is asking for it,

00:02:31.374 --> 00:02:33.438
or you do it because, you know,

00:02:33.438 --> 00:02:35.693
somebody in your family
is forcing you to do it.

00:02:35.693 --> 00:02:39.070
You don't actually do it because
you have a deep why for it

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.328
and so really important is
when you look at your goals,

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.908
attaching a strong why to each one.

00:02:44.908 --> 00:02:47.442
If you can't figure one
out, then drop the goal

00:02:47.442 --> 00:02:48.707
because you're never going to get it done.

00:02:48.707 --> 00:02:51.221
It's just going to
continue to be a wishlist

00:02:51.221 --> 00:02:52.980
and we want to move it from the wishlist

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:57.147
to actually a list of goals
that we're going to accomplish.

00:02:59.191 --> 00:03:01.908
Number three is take daily action.

00:03:01.908 --> 00:03:04.646
If this is important to you
that you accomplish this goal

00:03:04.646 --> 00:03:06.649
then you have to schedule it in daily.

00:03:06.649 --> 00:03:07.742
Look at your calendar

00:03:07.742 --> 00:03:10.581
and schedule time for it to happen daily.

00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:11.903
It doesn't have to be a ton of time.

00:03:11.903 --> 00:03:13.022
Doesn't mean that you now have

00:03:13.022 --> 00:03:14.809
five hours a day to spend on this,

00:03:14.809 --> 00:03:17.455
but everyday you need to
take some kind of action,

00:03:17.455 --> 00:03:18.656
even if it's small,

00:03:18.656 --> 00:03:21.253
at least half and hour,
moving forward on your goal,

00:03:21.253 --> 00:03:23.127
especially if you're doing this part time.

00:03:23.127 --> 00:03:25.415
You have a full-time job, you
have a family to take care of,

00:03:25.415 --> 00:03:26.745
you've got lots of demands for your time,

00:03:26.745 --> 00:03:28.341
you need to carve out the time.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:31.039
If you don't carve out the
time to accomplish your goals,

00:03:31.039 --> 00:03:33.055
the rest of your life will take over.

00:03:33.055 --> 00:03:35.943
It would happen there's this
theory of big rocks first.

00:03:35.943 --> 00:03:37.888
Image you've got sand, you've got pebbles

00:03:37.888 --> 00:03:39.856
and you've got big rocks.

00:03:39.856 --> 00:03:41.342
If you put the sand in first,

00:03:41.342 --> 00:03:43.882
and then the pebbles and you
put the big rocks into a jar,

00:03:43.882 --> 00:03:45.155
it won't all fit together.

00:03:45.155 --> 00:03:46.508
It's going to overflow.

00:03:46.508 --> 00:03:48.517
But if you put the big rocks in first,

00:03:48.517 --> 00:03:49.578
then the pebbles will come in

00:03:49.578 --> 00:03:52.272
and will fit around the big rocks,

00:03:52.272 --> 00:03:53.341
and then the sand will come in

00:03:53.341 --> 00:03:54.589
and fit around the pebbles

00:03:54.589 --> 00:03:56.423
and it will all fit into the jar.

00:03:56.423 --> 00:03:58.042
That jar is your schedule.

00:03:58.042 --> 00:03:59.840
If you're constantly just
doing the little things,

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.358
which is the sand and then the pebbles,

00:04:01.358 --> 00:04:02.983
you never have time to do the big things,

00:04:02.983 --> 00:04:04.504
which are your rocks.

00:04:04.504 --> 00:04:06.077
If this is important to you,

00:04:06.077 --> 00:04:08.318
then you put the big rocks in first.

00:04:08.318 --> 00:04:10.383
Adjust your calendar,
adjust your schedule,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.195
so that the things that
you want to accomplish,

00:04:12.195 --> 00:04:15.800
that are on that goal list,
are in your weekly calendar,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.899
so that you're doing
something consistently on it.

00:04:18.899 --> 00:04:20.210
And then the rest of life

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.658
will be the pebbles and sand

00:04:21.658 --> 00:04:23.530
and will find ways to take up your time,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.017
but you need to defend
that time in your calendar

00:04:26.017 --> 00:04:28.600
to work on the important goals.

00:04:31.402 --> 00:04:33.500
Number four is commit to somebody else.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.565
You're way more likely to
follow through on something

00:04:35.565 --> 00:04:36.873
when you commit to somebody else.

00:04:36.873 --> 00:04:39.723
When you tell a friend,
family member, a colleague,

00:04:39.723 --> 00:04:41.139
that you are going to do something,

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:43.053
you're much more likely to do it.

00:04:43.053 --> 00:04:44.460
You know, I told Jason
I'm going to be here

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.147
at 8:30 in the morning to film this video,

00:04:47.147 --> 00:04:49.172
I showed up here at 8:30 in the morning.

00:04:49.172 --> 00:04:51.803
When you don't commit to somebody else,

00:04:51.803 --> 00:04:54.195
when it's just you committing to yourself,

00:04:54.195 --> 00:04:56.377
you're really likely to let yourself down.

00:04:56.377 --> 00:04:59.876
We are not great accountability
partners for ourselves.

00:04:59.876 --> 00:05:02.635
We will let ourselves down constantly.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.740
And so when you can
commit to somebody else,

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.778
your chances of achieving
your goal go up dramatically.

00:05:07.778 --> 00:05:09.160
So you could do it through a buddy system,

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.807
you know, maybe have a spouse
that you want to do this with,

00:05:10.807 --> 00:05:12.422
maybe you have a friend that
you want to do this with,

00:05:12.422 --> 00:05:13.825
maybe there's somebody
else in your industry

00:05:13.825 --> 00:05:15.174
that you want to do this with,

00:05:15.174 --> 00:05:17.727
where you have your monthly
goals or weekly goals

00:05:17.727 --> 00:05:18.965
and you connect.

00:05:18.965 --> 00:05:20.287
You may do it through a mastermind group.

00:05:20.287 --> 00:05:22.104
That's what I do for myself.

00:05:22.104 --> 00:05:24.079
We've got eight people
in a mastermind group

00:05:24.079 --> 00:05:26.343
and we meet, physically, once per month

00:05:26.343 --> 00:05:27.875
to talk about our goals,

00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:29.025
and then every member is partnered up

00:05:29.025 --> 00:05:30.626
with somebody else in the group

00:05:30.626 --> 00:05:32.803
and every week you have
a phone call with them.

00:05:32.803 --> 00:05:34.945
It could be just 10, 15-minute
phone call once a week,

00:05:34.945 --> 00:05:38.281
to make sure that you do the things

00:05:38.281 --> 00:05:40.408
that you say you're going to do.

00:05:40.408 --> 00:05:41.784
So here's what I want to get done

00:05:41.784 --> 00:05:43.822
before our meeting next month.

00:05:43.822 --> 00:05:45.491
And then you have a weekly call

00:05:45.491 --> 00:05:49.487
to say how you're making
forward progress on it or not.

00:05:49.487 --> 00:05:51.402
And what you hate doing is
reporting to your partner

00:05:51.402 --> 00:05:53.073
that you didn't do it.

00:05:53.073 --> 00:05:55.019
And so having that weekly accountability

00:05:55.019 --> 00:05:57.492
helps makes sure that you're
making forward progress

00:05:57.492 --> 00:05:58.650
and sometimes that person

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.316
needs to hold your hand a little bit

00:06:00.316 --> 00:06:01.152
and sometimes that person

00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:03.414
needs to light a fire under
your butt a little bit.

00:06:03.414 --> 00:06:04.641
Just depends on the role.

00:06:04.641 --> 00:06:05.668
Depends where you're at.

00:06:05.668 --> 00:06:07.468
But having an accountability partner,

00:06:07.468 --> 00:06:09.430
committing to someone else
to say you're going to do it

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.874
and having them hold your
feet to the fire a little bit,

00:06:11.874 --> 00:06:16.041
helps make sure that you're
going to accomplish your goals.

00:06:17.719 --> 00:06:19.447
Number five is model success.

00:06:19.447 --> 00:06:20.866
One of my favorite things to do

00:06:20.866 --> 00:06:23.165
to accomplish any goal
is to model success.

00:06:23.165 --> 00:06:24.900
I find somebody who's already accomplished

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.470
what I want to do, figure
out what worked for them,

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.230
and then try it in my business.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.309
This is what saved my first company.

00:06:31.309 --> 00:06:33.468
At the beginning I had
to do everything myself.

00:06:33.468 --> 00:06:35.038
I tried to come up with
every new idea myself.

00:06:35.038 --> 00:06:36.738
I thought I was a creative person

00:06:36.738 --> 00:06:38.347
and I could solve this problem.

00:06:38.347 --> 00:06:39.490
And I could solve a lot of problems,

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:40.993
but you know what's even faster,

00:06:40.993 --> 00:06:43.171
is finding someone else
that's already solved it

00:06:43.171 --> 00:06:45.784
and then just tweak their
system to make it work for you.

00:06:45.784 --> 00:06:48.633
You know, Starbucks was
started because Howard Schultz

00:06:48.633 --> 00:06:52.457
went to Milan in Italy and
saw how the coffee shop

00:06:52.457 --> 00:06:54.694
was the center of life in Italy,

00:06:54.694 --> 00:06:57.057
it was the third home, between home, work,

00:06:57.057 --> 00:06:58.744
it was the third meeting spot.

00:06:58.744 --> 00:07:00.087
And he looked at North America and he saw

00:07:00.087 --> 00:07:01.747
like the Dunkin' Donuts of the world,

00:07:01.747 --> 00:07:03.013
where it's just in and out,

00:07:03.013 --> 00:07:05.225
you don't really spend any
time in a Dunkin' Donuts.

00:07:05.225 --> 00:07:07.343
And he said I want to bring
this Italian way of living

00:07:07.343 --> 00:07:10.065
to North America, and
then later to the world.

00:07:10.065 --> 00:07:11.233
And it worked.

00:07:11.233 --> 00:07:13.990
Like, all he did to build a
multi-billion dollar empire,

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.708
one of the biggest brands in the world,

00:07:15.708 --> 00:07:18.646
was model what worked
in a different market

00:07:18.646 --> 00:07:20.497
and brought it to North America.

00:07:20.497 --> 00:07:21.873
Whatever problem you're facing right now

00:07:21.873 --> 00:07:24.433
to achieving your goal,
somebody has already done it.

00:07:24.433 --> 00:07:25.496
Look to them.

00:07:25.496 --> 00:07:26.848
Understand their success.

00:07:26.848 --> 00:07:29.257
The bigger they are, the
easier it is to find out

00:07:29.257 --> 00:07:30.381
the early days, right.

00:07:30.381 --> 00:07:31.440
And that's what you want to figure out.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.357
How Howard Schultz opens
another Starbucks right now

00:07:34.357 --> 00:07:35.230
is not interesting.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.861
How he went from like zero to one,

00:07:36.861 --> 00:07:38.493
how did he build those first few stores,

00:07:38.493 --> 00:07:39.754
how did they make their first million,

00:07:39.754 --> 00:07:41.375
that is super interesting.

00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:42.641
And so that's what you need to model

00:07:42.641 --> 00:07:45.474
to help you accomplish your goals.

00:07:48.281 --> 00:07:50.104
Number six is bring on a team.

00:07:50.104 --> 00:07:51.376
As soon as you can afford it,

00:07:51.376 --> 00:07:52.736
you want to be able to bring on a team

00:07:52.736 --> 00:07:54.135
to help you accomplish your goal

00:07:54.135 --> 00:07:55.662
because the bigger the goal is,

00:07:55.662 --> 00:07:57.751
the more people you're going to need.

00:07:57.751 --> 00:07:59.513
And I think a lot of people
have it in their head

00:07:59.513 --> 00:08:00.990
that you need to hire somebody full time

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.510
and that's going to cost
X thousand dollars a year.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:04.488
You don't.

00:08:04.488 --> 00:08:06.208
The first guy I hired for my business,

00:08:06.208 --> 00:08:07.920
I hired for one hour a day.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.696
And that saved me more
than one hour a day of time

00:08:10.696 --> 00:08:13.829
because he was better at
doing the job than I was

00:08:13.829 --> 00:08:14.850
and it freed up my time

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.351
to go off and do more important things

00:08:16.351 --> 00:08:17.642
to help me build my business.

00:08:17.642 --> 00:08:19.738
So as soon as you're starting
to make any kind of money,

00:08:19.738 --> 00:08:21.383
it doesn't have to be a
lot of money, anything,

00:08:21.383 --> 00:08:22.954
I would take a good portion of that

00:08:22.954 --> 00:08:26.138
and invest it back into
bringing on somebody to help me,

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:29.231
even if it was for one hour a day,

00:08:29.231 --> 00:08:30.712
or a couple hours a week,

00:08:30.712 --> 00:08:33.527
so that you can make forward
momentum and forward progress.

00:08:33.527 --> 00:08:35.506
You can't do this alone.

00:08:35.506 --> 00:08:36.339
You can't.

00:08:36.339 --> 00:08:37.172
If you have a big goal,

00:08:37.172 --> 00:08:39.460
it's not going to happen with
just you doing everything

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:42.007
and so the faster you can get
used to bringing on a team,

00:08:42.007 --> 00:08:43.916
the better and also as a side benefit,

00:08:43.916 --> 00:08:45.925
helps build up your leadership skills

00:08:45.925 --> 00:08:48.188
so that you're getting
used to managing a team

00:08:48.188 --> 00:08:50.156
because you're going to
make a lot of mistakes too.

00:08:50.156 --> 00:08:51.442
If you've never managed people before,

00:08:51.442 --> 00:08:53.125
you're going to make a ton of mistakes,

00:08:53.125 --> 00:08:55.499
and better that it happens
on a really small scale

00:08:55.499 --> 00:08:57.304
and you learn from it and get better

00:08:57.304 --> 00:08:59.232
than if it really now becomes important

00:08:59.232 --> 00:09:00.492
because you've hired somebody full time

00:09:00.492 --> 00:09:02.075
and it has to work.

00:09:05.339 --> 00:09:07.196
And number seven is enjoy the process.

00:09:07.196 --> 00:09:08.804
I've talked about this
a lot on the channel.

00:09:08.804 --> 00:09:10.725
It has to be important to you

00:09:10.725 --> 00:09:12.955
that it's not just about
achieving the goal,

00:09:12.955 --> 00:09:15.844
but it's about enjoying the
work on the way to the goal.

00:09:15.844 --> 00:09:16.978
It's super important.

00:09:16.978 --> 00:09:19.427
You can only force yourself
to do something for so long

00:09:19.427 --> 00:09:21.701
before you give up and you quit.

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:24.083
If you don't enjoy the
work of what you're doing

00:09:24.083 --> 00:09:27.303
and your only goal is
achieving that outcome,

00:09:27.303 --> 00:09:28.329
you're going to fail.

00:09:28.329 --> 00:09:30.068
You're going to fail because
you don't enjoy the work.

00:09:30.068 --> 00:09:32.323
With the successful people
who are high achievers

